# Residue functionals I_ij of the families of curves used in two unrefereed preprints on the Hodge conjecture for
# Fermat varieties, each enclosed in a certified ball |I - c| <= r:
#   D35 I34: T. Peterson, The Hodge conjecture for Fermat varieties of degree 35, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.22945544 (v1.2),
#            Sec. 3 and App. A; published value 29.588332077128010399 - 6.7688877382028338180 i.
#   D44, D51A, D51B, D52A, D52B: the families prop:family44, prop:family51a, prop:family51b, prop:family52a and
#            prop:family52b of the E84HC release by Bhattacharjee, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.24055725 (v1.9.0), with the
#            residue functional in their sign convention.
# Made by code: an independent re-check written from the papers' definitions (not running their code), with mpmath
# interval arithmetic at 1300 bits: Newton from the published point, a Krawczyk test proving a unique zero in a box of
# radius 1e-95, the tangent vector enclosed the same way, and the residue sum enclosed in a complex box. Each line is a
# ball that contains that box: the centre to 80 digits and the radius rounded up (half-diagonal plus the rounding of the
# centre). Numbers only; no text of the sources is reproduced.
